  "title": "SI Base Quantities and Kinematics",
  "main_stem": null,
  "parts": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "In the following list, underline **all** quantities that are SI base quantities.\n\ncharge             electric current             force             time",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Under certain conditions, the distance $s$ moved in a straight line by an object in time $t$ is given by $$s = \\frac{1}{2}at^2$$ where $a$ is the acceleration of the object.\n\nState **two** conditions under which the above expression applies to the motion of the object.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)",
      "part_stem": "The variation with time $t$ of the velocity $v$ of a car that is moving in a straight line is shown in Fig. 1.1.",
      "text": "Fig. 1.1 [$v / \\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ against $t / \\mathrm{s}$: at $t = 0$, $v = -10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ rising linearly to $v = 0$ at $t = 4.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$, to $v = 10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ at $t = 8.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$, to $v = 20\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ at $t = 12.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$, then falling linearly to $v = 10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ at $t = 14.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$ and to $v = 0$ at $t = 16.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$.]",
      "marks": 0,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(i)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Compare, qualitatively, the acceleration of the car at time $t = 8.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$ and at time $t = 14.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$ in terms of:\n\n\u2022 magnitude\n\n\u2022 direction.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Determine the magnitude of the acceleration of the car at time $t = 4.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(iii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "The car is at point X at time $t = 0$.\n\nDetermine the magnitude of the displacement of the car from X at time $t = 12.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    }
  ],
  "markscheme": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "only electric current **and** time underlined"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "initial speed / velocity is zero"
        },
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "(non-zero magnitude of) acceleration is constant / uniform (and in a straight line)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(i)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "magnitude of acceleration at $t = 8.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$ is less than that at $t = 14.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "direction of acceleration at $t = 8.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$ is opposite to that at $t = 14.0\\,\\mathrm{s}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(ii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$a =$ gradient **or** $a = (v-u) / t$ **or** $a = \\Delta v / (\\Delta)t$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$a =$ e.g. $(20 + 10) / 12$ **or** $(0 + 10) / 4$ **or** $(20 - 0) / (12 - 4)$; $a = 2.5\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(iii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "displacement $= [\\frac{1}{2} \\times (12 - 4) \\times 20] - [\\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 10]$ **or** displacement $= (-10 \\times 12) + (\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2.5 \\times 12^{2})$ **or** displacement $= (20 \\times 12) - (\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2.5 \\times 12^{2})$ **or** displacement $= \\frac{1}{2} \\times (20 - 10) \\times 12$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "displacement $= 60\\,\\mathrm{m}$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
